  "prefLabel": "Env-Wq 1602.05 Beneficial use",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Env-Wq 1602.05 “Beneficial use” means taking advantage of the nutrient content and soil conditioning properties, or both, of septage by supplying agronomic and soil conditioning benefits such as the nitrogen, phosphorus, micronutrients, or organic matter needs for a crop, forested land, or a nursery. Beneficial use includes land application at approved agronomic rates.\n\nSource. (See Revision Note #1 and Revision Note #2 at chapter heading for Env-Wq 1600) #13944, eff 4-27-24",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/env-wq1600.html"
}
